1. Privacy, GDPR and Data Minimisation

Data Collection
The AI Failures Museum system uses Django's built-in User model and collects the following personal data:

Data collected:
- Username
- Email address
- Password
- First Name
- Last Name
- Account creation timestamp
- Last login timestamp
- Account status flags

This ensures that no sensitive personal data, location tracking, payment information or third-party analytics information is stored.

Legal Basis (GDPR)
- Consent: Users consent when creating accounts

User Rights (GDPR)
Users have the following rights, implementable vis Django's admin interface:
- Access: View their data through Django admin
- Rectification: Edit username, email, first name and last name
- Erasure: Delete account via Django admin

